---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Cta from '../components/Cta.astro';
import { site } from '../lib/site';
import { cover, alt } from '../lib/images';

const jsonLd = [{
  '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
  itemListElement: [
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: `${site.url}/` },
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'About', item: `${site.url}/about/` },
  ],
}];
---
<Base title="About Bloomridge Springs" description="A small child-development centre in Banasree, Dhaka, built around one idea: every child belongs, every child blooms. Who we are, what we believe, and why the classroom is small on purpose." ogImage="centre-exterior" jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <section class="band band--paper">
    <div class="wrap split">
      <div>
        <p class="kicker">About the centre</p>
        <h1>Small on purpose</h1>
        <p class="lead">Bloomridge Springs is a child-development centre on a quiet lane in Banasree, for children aged {site.ages.min} to {site.ages.max}. We keep the classroom to {site.seats} seats so that every child is known by every adult in the room.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="arch">
        <Image src={cover('centre-exterior')} alt={alt['centre-exterior']} widths={[600, 900, 1400]} sizes="(min-width: 56rem) 45vw, 100vw" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <h2>What we believe</h2>
      <p>Every child is unique in their strengths and their challenges, so there is no one-size-fits-all method here. The program adapts to the child; the child does not have to fit into a rigid box.</p>
      <p>We do not diagnose, and we do not wait for a diagnosis. We look at what your child can do today, in six areas of development, and build from there. Where a paediatrician or developmental specialist should be involved, we say so plainly.</p>
      <p>We believe the hard part is not knowing what to do. It is doing it consistently, across the therapy room, the classroom and the home. That is why our whole way of working is built around one living Student Profile and a daily loop between the adults in your child’s life. <a href="/how-we-work/">Here is how that works.</a></p>

      <h2>Who is in the room</h2>
      <p>An occupational therapist, a speech and language therapist, special educators and classroom teachers, with a child psychologist leading the weekly group session. They share a staff room, a profile for each child, and a habit of talking at the end of every day.</p>
      <p>Names and profiles of the current team are available at the centre and at your first visit.</p>

      <h2>Where we are</h2>
      <p>{site.address.full}. First floor, on a quiet residential lane, a short rickshaw ride from Rampura bridge. <a href="/contact/">Directions and contact details.</a></p>

      <h2>The name</h2>
      <p>A spring is where growth begins, and a ridge is a place with a view. Our mark, a B with a bloom and a leaf inside it, says the rest: every child belongs, every child blooms.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Cta />
</Base>
